Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Keyboard light info in Settings > Keyboard

Adds a read-only Keyboard light row under Settings > System > Keyboard.
The Zinwa Q25 keyboard firmware owns its backlight and ignores host
writes to the backlight register, so Settings offers no switch or
slider: the row says how to use the keyboard's own keys (Sym+0 toggles
the light; with the PaBaLF firmware, Sym+Shift+1 to 9 sets the level).

The row is shown only when ro.sable.keyboard_backlight is true, which
the Q25 layer sets, and is found by searching for keyboard light,
backlight or kb light.
---
 .../sable_keyboard_backlight_strings.xml      | 23 +++++++++
 res/xml/keyboard_settings.xml                 | 11 +++++
 ...KeyboardBacklightPreferenceController.java | 47 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 81 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 res/values/sable_keyboard_backlight_strings.xml
 create mode 100644 src/com/android/settings/sable/SableKeyboardBacklightPreferenceController.java

diff --git a/res/values/sable_keyboard_backlight_strings.xml b/res/values/sable_keyboard_backlight_strings.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2f9fa92
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/values/sable_keyboard_backlight_strings.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
